\node[below right] at (5.3,4.15) {$C$};
\draw[black,dashed] (3,0)--(3,3)--(0,3);
\fill[black] (3,3) circle (1.5pt);
\node[above left] at (3,3) {$(30,180)$};
\draw[black,dashed] (5,0)--(5,5)--(0,5);
\draw[black,dashed] (5,4)--(0,4);
\fill[black] (5,5) circle (1.5pt);
\fill[black] (5,4) circle (1.5pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(a) The revenue and cost lines intersect at $(30,180)$. Break-even is $30$ snack packs, with revenue of $\$180$.

(b) At $n=50$, the graph gives $R=300$ and $C=240$.
$\begin{align*}P&=R-C\\&=300-240\\&=60\end{align*}$
The profit is $\$60$.

