The lines intersect at $(40, 200)$.
Break-even point is $40$ smoothies at $\$200$.
At $n = 70$:
$R = 5(70) = 350$
$C = 100 + 2.5(70) = 275$
$P = R - C = 350 - 275 = 75$
Selling $70$ smoothies yields a profit of $\$75$.

